From: Caner Altinbasak <cal@brightsign.biz>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:42:05 +0100
Subject: fix: promote video hole for diagonal reflection transforms OS-22131

OverlayStrategyUnderlayBrightsign::Propose built its
OverlayCandidateFactory context with supports_mask_filter only, leaving
supports_flip_rotate_transform at its default of false.
FromVideoHoleQuad feeds that flag to GetOverlayTransform, which maps the
two diagonal reflections to FLIP_VERTICAL_CLOCKWISE_90/270 only when it
is set and otherwise returns OVERLAY_TRANSFORM_INVALID.

As a result the kVideoHole quad failed as not-axis-aligned for
mirror_rot90 and mirror_rot270, so no candidate was proposed, Attempt
and VideoHoleDraw never ran, vid_player_set_geometry was never called
and the player was hidden.  The hole punched in the graphics plane then
composited as a solid black rectangle.

The video plane applies the orientation itself via the firmware
Transposer, so all eight orientations are overlayable.  Set the flag
explicitly; the base class derives it from a capability checker that is
private and defaults to false on this platform.

diff --git a/components/viz/service/display/overlay_strategy_underlay_brightsign.cc b/components/viz/service/display/overlay_strategy_underlay_brightsign.cc
index 5cfcbf2d85327f35abf08e209bc9ca8cfb8de137..df862b6e963d3b0fbab0e5fcb480863271290941 100644
--- a/components/viz/service/display/overlay_strategy_underlay_brightsign.cc
+++ b/components/viz/service/display/overlay_strategy_underlay_brightsign.cc
@@ -301,6 +301,11 @@ void OverlayStrategyUnderlayBrightsign::Propose(
     auto overlay_iter = quad_list.end();
     OverlayCandidateFactory::OverlayContext context;
     context.supports_mask_filter = true;
+    // The video plane applies the orientation itself (firmware Transposer), so all eight
+    // orientations are overlayable. Without this the diagonal reflections (mirror_rot90 /
+    // mirror_rot270) yield OVERLAY_TRANSFORM_INVALID, the video hole is never promoted and
+    // it renders black instead (OS-22131).
+    context.supports_flip_rotate_transform = true;
     OverlayCandidateFactory candidate_factory = OverlayCandidateFactory(
         render_pass, resource_provider, surface_damage_rect_list,
         &output_color_matrix, GetPrimaryPlaneDisplayRect(primary_plane), context);
